max-visits: 36
is-card: true
card-image: img/flags.jpg
frequency: 100
tags: party_affairs

= Campaigning

Our voters have less and less confidence in us. Who shall we reassure?

- @workers: The urban working class, our traditional support base.
- @new_middle: The "new middle class" of government employees and white-collar workers.
- @old_middle: The "old middle class" of small independent businessmen and artisans.
- @rural: Rural workers and small farmers, who have felt neglected by us in the past.
- @unemployed: The unemployed.
- @christians: Christians, who typically support the EPP.
- @root: We either don't want to or cannot campaign right now.
- @easy_discard

@workers
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: workers_spd += 6*(1-dissent); workers_spd -= 2 if unemployed >= 15; workers_spd -= 2 if unemployed >= 25; workers_spd += 6*(1-dissent) if wtb_adopted = 1; resources -= 1; workers_spd += 3*(1-dissent) if nationalization_progress >= 1; workers_spd -=4 if accelerationism >= 50; 

We have increased our campaigning among the workers. [? if unemployed >= 15: The high levels of unemployment make our campaign more difficult. ?][? if wtb_adopted = 1 : Adopting the WTB plan gives us a new rallying point around which to attract workers. ?][? if accelerationism >= 50 : The working class wants to break their deadlock, bringing a new future by having to out-accelerate capital. Gluttony enslaves their mind as they watch people from other countries eat endlessly. **Hope falls.** ?] 

@new_middle
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: new_middle_spd += 6*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd -= 4 if socialism <= 49 and peoples_party == 0; resources -= 1; peoples_party_support += 1; new_middle_spd -=6 if accelerationism >= 40;

We have increased our campaigning among the new middle class. [? if socialism <= 49 and peoples_party == 0: The popular antipathy towards socialism among this group makes our campaign more difficult. ?] [? if peoples_party > 0: As a people's party, we have an easier time increasing support among the middle class than before. ?] [? if accelerationism >= 40: The middle class has seen the truth, and nothing human makes it out of the near future. They set to give up, with sloth blinding their eyes. **Hope falls.** ?]

@old_middle
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: old_middle_spd += 5*(1-dissent); resources -= 1; old_middle_spd -= 3 if nationalism >= 51 and peoples_party == 0; peoples_party_support += 1; old_middle_spd -=10 if accelerationism >= 10;

We have increased our campaigning among the old middle class. [? if nationalism >= 51 and peoples_party == 0: The high levels of nationalism among this group make our campaign more difficult. ?] [? if peoples_party > 0: As a people's party, we have an easier time increasing support among the middle class than before. ?] [? if accelerationism >= 10: The bourgeousie fall into madness as they realize machines must become aware, that post-humanism is the key to self-awareness and unlimited growth. Their greed swells endlessly. **Hope falls.** ?]

@rural
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: rural_spd += 5*(1-dissent); rural_spd -= 3*(1-dissent) if peoples_party == 0; resources -= 1; peoples_party_support += 1; rural_spd += 3*(1-dissent) if rural_policy >= 2; rural_spd -= 6 if accelerationism >= 20;

We have increased our campaigning among farmers. [? if peoples_party == 0: We have not historically campaigned much among the farmers, and they do not trust us. ?][? if peoples_party > 0: As a people's party, we have an easier time increasing support among farmers than before. ?][? if rural_policy >= 2 : Our rural policies have made it easier for us to build support among farmers. ?] [? if accelerationism >= 10: The farmers smile as they rose from the ground. They did not want to be human. They wanted to go faster, envy to others with better lives. **Hope falls.** ?]

@unemployed
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: unemployed_spd += 6*(1-dissent); resources -= 1; unemployed_spd -= 3 if welfare < 0; unemployed_spd += 6*(1-dissent) if wtb_adopted = 1; unemployed_spd += 3*(1-dissent) if welfare >= 2; unemployed_spd -= 6 if accelerationism >= 30;

We have increased our campaigning among the unemployed. [? if welfare < 0: The welfare cuts and resultant poverty make our campaign more difficult, since we are associated with the government that enacted these cuts, and our campaign may even backfire. ?][? if wtb_adopted = 1 : Adopting the WTB plan gives us a new rallying point around which to attract support from the unemployed. ?] [? if accelerationism >= 30: The poor and starving cannot save the broken system. Their wrath will bring it down, collapse be their path forward. Can you hear them sing? **Hope falls.** ?]

@christians
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
view-if: peoples_party == 1
on-arrival: christians_spd += 6*(1-dissent); resources -= 1; christians_spd -=8 if accelerationism >= 40;

We have increased our campaigning among Christians. [? if accelerationism >= 40: The christians begin their holy work further, pushing past the constraints imposed by their heretical capitalist beliefs. They pride themselves on the new social relations that will shatter the world. **Hope falls.** ?]
